explanation:
    The nucleus is the tiny centre of the atom. Protons and neutrons are in it. The electrons are outside.

item u1-l2-match-particles
type: match
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-ch2

prompt:
    Match each particle to its charge.

pairs:
    {"id":"proton","left":"Proton","right":"Positive"}
    {"id":"neutron","left":"Neutron","right":"No charge"}
    {"id":"electron","left":"Electron","right":"Negative"}

explanation:
    Protons are positive, neutrons have no charge and electrons are negative.

item u1-l2-sort-location
type: sort
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-ch2

prompt:
    Where is each particle? Sort them.

buckets:
    {"id":"in","label":"In the nucleus","icon":"AqNucleus"}
    {"id":"out","label":"Outside the nucleus","icon":"AqOrbit"}

items:
    {"id":"proton","label":"Proton","bucket":"in"}
    {"id":"neutron","label":"Neutron","bucket":"in"}
    {"id":"electron","label":"Electron","bucket":"out"}

explanation:
    Protons and neutrons are in the nucleus. Electrons are outside it.

item u1-x-negative
type: choice
surfaces: practice
surfaces: checkpoint
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-ch2

prompt:
    Which particle has a negative electric charge?

options:
    {"id":"electron","label":"The electron"}
    {"id":"proton","label":"The proton","note":"Protons are positive."}
    {"id":"neutron","label":"The neutron","note":"Neutrons have no charge."}

answer: electron

explanation:
    Electrons are negative. Protons are positive and neutrons have no charge.

item u1-x-neutron-charge
type: true_or_myth
surfaces: practice
surfaces: checkpoint
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-ch2

statement:
    Neutrons have no electric charge.

answer: true

explanation:
    True. That is why they are called neutrons.
